description:
Change under review: mark orders as paid when the payment provider calls our webhook. Added files are shown in full.

`src/payments/verify.ts` (added):
```ts
1 import { createHmac, timingSafeEqual } from "node:crypto";
2 import { secrets } from "../config/secrets.js";
3
4 export async function verifyWebhookSignature(rawBody: string, header: string | null): Promise<boolean> {
5   if (header === null) return false;
6   const key = await secrets.get("payments-webhook-signing-key");
7   const expected = createHmac("sha256", key).update(rawBody).digest();
8   const given = Buffer.from(header, "hex");
9   return given.length === expected.length && timingSafeEqual(given, expected);
10 }
```

`src/routes/payment-webhook.ts` (added):
```ts
1 import { orders } from "../db/orders.js";
2 import { verifyWebhookSignature } from "../payments/verify.js";
3
4 export async function paymentWebhook(req: Request): Promise<Response> {
5   const rawBody = await req.text();
6   const valid = verifyWebhookSignature(rawBody, req.headers.get("x-signature"));
7   if (!valid) {
8     return new Response("bad signature", { status: 401 });
9   }
10   const event = JSON.parse(rawBody);
11   if (event.type === "payment.succeeded") {
12     await orders.markPaid(event.data.orderId);
13   }
14   return new Response(null, { status: 204 });
15 }
```

The webhook route is public, as the payment provider requires; the signature is the only thing that authenticates a call. `secrets.get` reads the signing key from the secrets manager.
